{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007273-hedge-and-the-dream","id":1007273,"title":"Hedge and the Dream","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-23T08:44:42-08:00","id":1007273,"title":"Hedge and the Dream","content":"Having skimmed through the open development of the Hedge in Changeling the Dreaming, it appears that the Hedge draws from the dreams of the people in the area. Could it have some connection to the Dream realms accessible by Mages?. <br /> <br /> Since we have a while to wait for the Crossover Chronicle book, I was wondering if anyone had some ideas on what that connection might be?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9255-docsteve2020","name":"DocSteve2020","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T08:52:59-08:00","id":1007277,"title":"","content":"I always figured the relationship between the Hedge and the Astral Oneiros was sort of like the relationship between the fallen world and twilight. Things that happen in one can and do affect the other, but only ever subtly unless there are some intelligent beings of power involved. I guess I sort of viewed it as a ring with Fallen &lt;-&gt; Astral Oneiros &lt;-&gt; Hedge &lt;-&gt; Fallen. I'd be interested to know what other people thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T09:03:57-08:00","id":1007280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DocSteve2020</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007273-hedge-and-the-dream#post1007273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having skimmed through the open development of the Hedge in Changeling the Dreaming, it appears that the Hedge draws from the dreams of the people in the area. Could it have some connection to the Dream realms accessible by Mages?. <br /> <br /> Since we have a while to wait for the Crossover Chronicle book, I was wondering if anyone had some ideas on what that connection might be?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Hedge is related to the Astral then it's the very shallow edge of it. Changelings can't do much more than get their feet wet in the Astral waters. They can't venture past the First Reversal or the realms past that point. Their weirdo powers though do allow them to do some stuff with dreams that would leave a Mage confused despite the ability Mages have to also enter the dreams of the slumbering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T09:24:38-08:00","id":1007285,"title":"","content":"<br /> While just a personal theory and not something official, I think <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/988291-werewolves-and-the-astral-wat-do?p=989302#post989302\">this</a> is interesting enough to link in this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T09:41:46-08:00","id":1007291,"title":"","content":"Dreams are all things that Mages can reach using Mind magic. The Hedge and Arcadia beyond have nothing to do with the Astral, and changelings don't have the ability to muck around in the Oneiros, the &quot;Dream Realm&quot; of the Astral-or, as it's been more accurately revealed, the Realm of Individual Human Souls. Changelings don't directly meddle with souls.<br /> <br /> Simply put, no, the Hedge and the Oneiros aren't the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T12:05:37-08:00","id":1008232,"title":"","content":"I like to think that the soul &quot;feeds&quot; the mind with raw material to construct dreams, but do not generate them by itself. That helps me sort between mind and soul in my own headcanon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T17:15:42-08:00","id":1009094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1007273-hedge-and-the-dream?p=1007291#post1007291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dreams are all things that Mages can reach using Mind magic. The Hedge and Arcadia beyond have nothing to do with the Astral, and changelings don't have the ability to muck around in the Oneiros, the &amp;quot;Dream Realm&amp;quot; of the Astral-or, as it's been more accurately revealed, the Realm of Individual Human Souls. Changelings don't directly meddle with souls.<br /> <br /> Simply put, no, the Hedge and the Oneiros aren't the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, but also Dreams amd the Oneiros DO intersect. A Dream is a an expression of the soul, and so the Dream is a sliver of the soul/Oneiros. But while mages and other dreamers are swimming in a stream that eventually flows into the larger Astral Realms, a changeling is wading ankle deep in the stream. They can't swim out to sea/the Astral but the fish in the stream (usually) can't step up onto the bank/into the Hedge either- even if the water from their dreams waters the grass on the bank and makes it grow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T17:16:35-08:00","id":1009095,"title":"","content":"Whoops. Double post <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10769,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","user":"LLegume","date":".  Double post... 11-27-2016, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T02:03:44-08:00","id":1009242,"title":"","content":"It's more that you can see someone's thoughts when you're in their Oneiros, which when they're asleep means you can see their dreams. I describe it in a forthcoming Beast book as like seeing sunlight from underwater.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T12:44:35-08:00","id":1009435,"title":"","content":"So the Astral Barrier forms the water's surface? I like this imagery. I like it a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}